# ESLint and Obsidian lint conventions

CI runs `npm run lint` with `--max-warnings 0`. Generated and edited code must satisfy these rules. Do not add inline `eslint-disable`; accepted exceptions go only in `eslint.suppressions.json`.

## DOM

- Prefer Obsidian helpers: `createEl` / `.createEl` over `document.createElement` (including `canvas`).
- Never set a native `title` attribute (browser tooltip). Use `aria-label` and/or `LabelTooltip`.

## Parsing and vision

- Parse note / base / bundle YAML only via `parseNoteYaml` — never import `parseYaml` from Obsidian or the `yaml` package.
- In `vision/` and `pixi/lighting/`, do not read `vision.enabled` or import/use `visionOn` except in the allowed askers (`sightSources` / `selectSight` and `tokenSightPolicy`).

## Shared helpers

- Shared helper modules must not import plugin or host APIs (`obsidian`, Electron, CodeMirror, Node builtins, plugin-only paths). See `scripts/boundaries.mjs`.

## TypeScript and i18n

- Annotate function return types explicitly.
- UI copy goes through `t(...)`. English under `locales/en/` is the source of truth; keep `locales/ru/` in sync when adding keys.

## Before finishing

- After substantive edits under linted paths, run `npm run lint` and fix warnings before considering the work done.
- `lint:scan` scorecard findings are not the CI gate; do not churn the whole repo for them unless asked.
